{
  // The production entrypoints `scripts/worker.ts` and `scripts/scheduler.ts`
  // are EXCLUDED from tsconfig.json (see its "exclude"), and CI's only
  // typecheck runs `tsc --noEmit` with no -p, so it uses that root config.
  // Nothing imports these files either — every reference to them is a string
  // inside a guard test — so they cannot be pulled into the program
  // transitively. Result: the two processes that run the queue in production
  // have never been typechecked. This config exists to typecheck exactly them.
  //
  // Keep it a SEPARATE program rather than deleting "scripts" from the root
  // exclude: the rest of scripts/ is one-off operational tooling that does not
  // hold to the app's strictness, and folding it in would make this a
  // migration instead of a gate. Refs #806.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // The root config is `incremental`; a second program sharing its default
    // .tsbuildinfo would make the two invocations clobber each other's cache.
    "incremental": false
  },
  "include": [
    // The repo declares its own ambient globals — `src/types/globals.d.ts:20`
    // has `var EdgeRuntime: string | undefined`, which `src/lib/prisma.ts`
    // branches on. The root config picks that up incidentally via its blanket
    // `**/*.ts`; a scoped program does not, and omitting it fails with two
    // TS2304 "Cannot find name 'EdgeRuntime'" errors in a file that has
    // nothing to do with these scripts. Verified by removing this line.
    "src/types/**/*.d.ts",

    // ── The production entrypoints ───────────────────────────────────────
    "scripts/worker.ts",
    "scripts/scheduler.ts",
    // `seed.ts` is one too, and was missed: production seeding runs
    // `dist/seed.mjs`, which `build:seed` bundles from this file (see the
    // "Knowledge-base / RAG seeding" section of CLAUDE.md). It met the
    // criterion already written down here and simply was not listed.
    "scripts/seed.ts",

    // ── Scripts that WRITE to a database (#1485) ─────────────────────────
    //
    // The comment above says the rest of `scripts/` "does not hold to the
    // app's strictness, and folding it in would make this a migration". That
    // premise was measured and is mostly false: of the 18 scripts that can
    // modify data, 15 passed this program unchanged and the 3 that failed were
    // not strictness mismatches but BROKEN SCRIPTS —
    //
    //   seed-staging.ts   called `hashForLookup` with no import; threw
    //                     ReferenceError at step 2. Fixed.
    //   seed-demo.ts      `billingAccount.create` missing the required
    //                     `stripeCustomerId`; threw every time into a
    //                     swallowing catch, so the plan differentiator never
    //                     happened. Fixed.
    //   itest-spray.ts    imports `importLocationSpatialFile`, which #40
    //                     renamed and made off-thread. Broken since then, and
    //                     a rework rather than a rename. Excluded; filed as
    //                     #1659.
    //
    // The criterion is WRITES, not runs-in-production, and for a type error
    // the two are the same class: either way it surfaces when somebody runs
    // the thing against live data, with no earlier signal. The difference is
    // that a broken worker fails loudly on a schedule somebody watches, while
    // a broken backfill fails once, in front of an operator, mid-incident.
    //
    // `tests/guards/data-writing-scripts-are-typechecked.test.ts` DERIVES this
    // set from the filesystem and fails when a new data-writing script is
    // absent — a curated list is a list somebody forgets (#805).
    "scripts/add-tenant-owner.ts",
    "scripts/add-test-user.ts",
    "scripts/backfill-journal-title-descriptors.ts",
    "scripts/backfill-news-tags.ts",
    "scripts/import-crop-varieties.ts",
    "scripts/import-knowledge.ts",
    "scripts/import-products.ts",
    "scripts/import-units.ts",
    "scripts/migrate-files-to-cloud.ts",
    "scripts/rag/corpus.ts",
    "scripts/rag/ingest-satellite-guide.ts",
    "scripts/rag/ingest-tenant.ts",
    "scripts/retire-sample-products.ts",
    "scripts/seed-agri-events.ts",
    "scripts/seed-demo.ts",
    "scripts/seed-promotions.ts",
    "scripts/seed-staging.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules"
  ]
}
